# Lean & Maintainable Code Bar

## Minimal Changes

- Make the smallest change that solves the problem
- One concern per PR; no drive-by refactors
- No extra abstractions, layers, or indirection unless they pay for themselves

## Human-Readable

- Clear names over short names
- Obvious control flow over clever patterns
- Readable beats clever; future-you is the audience

## Comments

- Only where intent isn't obvious from the code itself
- Explain *why*, not *what*

## Dependencies

- Prefer fixing or pinning over large upgrades
- Upgrade dependencies only when the task explicitly calls for modernization
